<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tetricus I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 280</span> · Also known as Gaius Pius Esuvius Tetricus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tetricus I was the last emperor of the breakaway <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallic-empire">Gallic Empire</a>, ruling from 271 to 274. A senator and governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallia-aquitania">Aquitania</a>, he was proclaimed after the murder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victorinus">Victorinus</a>. In 274 he was defeated by the emperor Aurelian near Châlons, reportedly abandoning his army, and he and his son were led in Aurelian's triumph but then pardoned and given an office in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tetricus-i.jpg" alt="Tetricus I" width="320" height="307" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: АНО &quot;Международный нумизматический клуб&quot; · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:INC-2045-a_%D0%90%D1%83%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%83%D1%81._%D0%A2%D0%B5%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BA_I_%D0%A1%D1%82%D0%B0%D1%80%D1%88%D0%B8%D0%B9._%D0%9E%D0%BA._271%E2%80%94274_%D0%B3%D0%B3._(%D0%B0%D0%B2%D0%B5%D1%80%D1%81).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
